<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Workflow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <Workflow> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        NEW FILE, 2026-09-01. LOI__c had no workflow metadata before this change. W1 of the LOI
        approval cutover (agent-output/loi-approval-cutover-design.md), which moves the principal
        LOI approval OFF Opportunity.LOI_Approval and ONTO the LOI__c record itself. Direct sibling
        of workflows/Underwriting__c.workflow-meta.xml (2026-08-28) — same shape, same reasoning,
        different object.

        🔴 UPDATED 2026-09-02, item 1 of agent-output/three-gaps-design-2026-09-02.md, DECISION D-1
        = OPTION L-A (reuse LOI_Status__c as the pending-hide flag, rather than adding a new
        Checkbox). THREE FIELD UPDATES ADDED: LOI_Status_Pending, LOI_Status_Rejected,
        LOI_Status_Recalled. All four field updates in this file (including the pre-existing
        LOI_Status_Approved) are fired ONLY by approvalProcesses/LOI__c.LOI_Approval, as
        initialSubmissionActions / finalApprovalActions / finalRejectionActions / recallActions
        respectively. Do not add a <rules> element: an active rule writing LOI_Status__c on an
        ordinary edit would fake an approval.

        🔴 THE REJECTION FIELD UPDATE BELOW (LOI_Status_Rejected) IS A DELIBERATE, DOCUMENTED
        REVISION OF USER DECISION D-3 FROM THE LOI APPROVAL CUTOVER DESIGN (2026-09-01), NOT AN
        OVERSIGHT OF IT. D-3's SUBSTANCE, QUOTED THERE AS "The LOI stage will remain on Under
        review after rejection" — i.e. NO Stage__c rewind — IS STILL TRUE AND UNCHANGED; nothing
        here writes Stage__c. What changes is LOI_Status__c ONLY: the three-gaps design (§2.1)
        named this a "free rejection marker" — today a rejection changes nothing anywhere and only
        the approval history records it; item 1's four-exit rule (submit/approve/reject/recall must
        each leave LOI_Status__c somewhere sane, because the pending-hide criterion on
        flexipages/LOI_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml keys off this exact field) forces a rejection
        write to exist, so the LOI cutover design's own §5.2 "cheap, in-scope gain" is taken here.
        The retired Opportunity.LOI_Approval's Set_Stage_Underwriting rejection rewind (a full
        Stage__c move, LOI -> Underwriting) is STILL not rebuilt and stays an accepted, documented
        loss — see LoiApprovalStampService.cls's own header for why an Apex substitute was
        rejected (it would newly have to satisfy NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression and
        No_Backward_Stage_Movement, which the old approval's field update bypassed). Only the
        picklist value changes; the stage lock/rewind story is untouched.

        🔴 RECALL WRITES 'Draft', AND THIS IS A KNOWN, ACCEPTED INFORMATION LOSS — USER DECISION,
        three-gaps design §2.1/§7 D-1: "on recall, write Draft and accept the clobber." A
        workflow field update writes a LITERAL; it cannot restore whatever LOI_Status__c held
        before submission. If the LOI had been countered (CounterOfferService.cls writes
        LOI_Status__c = 'Countered'), a recall after that counter round silently overwrites
        'Countered' with 'Draft'. Approval history still shows the counter and the recall
        separately; only the picklist value on the record itself loses the distinction. This was
        shown to the user before being chosen over adding a second, lossless Checkbox field.

        WHY THIS RECORD'S OWN FIELD, NOT THE PARENT'S. This is the child-object half of moving the
        approval onto LOI__c. Every field update here writes only this record's own field —
        required, because LOI__c.Opportunity__c is a Lookup, so an approval process on this object
        cannot field-update the parent Opportunity at all. The parent mirror
        (Opportunity.LOI_Approved__c) is written separately by flows/LOI_Approval_Sync.flow-meta.xml,
        entry-scoped on LOI_Status__c transitioning to 'Approved' (recordTriggerType = Update,
        doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria = true — both load-bearing, see that flow's own
        header and LoiApprovalStampService.cls's "THE TRIGGERING MARKER (D-4)" section for the
        251-record bulk callers this exact pair of settings keeps immune), calling
        LoiApprovalStampService. Writing 'Pending Approval' on submission and 'Rejected' /
        'Draft' on rejection/recall does NOT fire that flow — it only fires on a transition INTO
        'Approved' — so the parent-mirror chain is unaffected by any of the three new field
        updates below.

        DEPLOY ORDER — LOAD-BEARING. This file must land in the SAME deploy as (or before)
        approvalProcesses/LOI__c.LOI_Approval.approvalProcess-meta.xml, which references all four
        field updates below BY NAME and cannot deploy otherwise — the same requirement
        Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval's header records at its own deploy-order note.
    -->
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>LOI_Status_Approved</fullName>
        <description>Final approval action of LOI__c.LOI_Approval. Sets LOI Status to Approved on this LOI record. Consumed by flows/LOI_Approval_Sync, which mirrors the transition onto the parent deal.</description>
        <field>LOI_Status__c</field>
        <literalValue>Approved</literalValue>
        <name>LOI Status Approved</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>LOI_Status_Pending</fullName>
        <description>Initial submission action of LOI__c.LOI_Approval. Sets LOI Status to Pending Approval. Activates LOI_Record_Page Submit for Approval's second criterion, hiding the button while true, and lights the amber badge in lwc/dealDocStatus.</description>
        <field>LOI_Status__c</field>
        <literalValue>Pending Approval</literalValue>
        <name>LOI Status Pending</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>LOI_Status_Recalled</fullName>
        <description>Recall action of LOI__c.LOI_Approval. Sets LOI Status back to Draft, restoring Submit for Approval visibility. Writes a literal - a prior 'Countered' value is lost. Accepted, user-decided loss; see this file's header.</description>
        <field>LOI_Status__c</field>
        <literalValue>Draft</literalValue>
        <name>LOI Status Recalled</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>LOI_Status_Rejected</fullName>
        <description>Final rejection action of LOI__c.LOI_Approval. Sets LOI Status to Rejected. Does NOT move Stage__c - LOI stays at Under Review, per decision D-3 in the LOI approval cutover design. Gives rejection a visible effect; see this file's header.</description>
        <field>LOI_Status__c</field>
        <literalValue>Rejected</literalValue>
        <name>LOI Status Rejected</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
</Workflow>
